Values from ePrint 2026/2521
============================

Source: Shiduo Zhang, Paul Kirchner, Xiuhan Lin, Yang Yu, "Efficient Fixed-Point Implementation of Mitaka", IACR
ePrint 2026/2521, 2026.

How they are used:

- Table 2 (p. 9): the parameters of Mitaka-512 and Mitaka-1024 (the security parameter, the ring degree, the NTRU
  modulus, the trapdoor quality parameter, the smoothing error, the denominators p_u and p_A, the perturbation
  scaling factor, the widths s and r) are the definitions Params.mitaka512 and Params.mitaka1024
  (Mitaka/Sampler.lean), eps512 and eps1024 (Mitaka/Table2.lean), and constants of the theorems in
  Mitaka/Lemma5.lean, Mitaka/Table2.lean, Mitaka/FixedPointCentre.lean, Mitaka/Witness.lean and
  Mitaka/Headline.lean. The measured failure probabilities per attempt enter the call budgets of the theorems
  headline_tableRate_mitaka512 and headline_tableRate_mitaka1024 (Mitaka/Headline.lean).
- Algorithm 4 and Table 4 (p. 12-13): the constants q = 12289, b in {43, 44}, t in {0, 16} and the bounds of
  Table 4 are the definitions of Mitaka/Algorithm4.lean (Algorithm4.q, Algorithm4.Table4Input).
- Comments in the Lean files, README.md and LIMITS.md quote short statements of the paper, with page and line
  numbers, to identify what each Lean statement formalises.

The theorems of this repository are proved in Lean from these values; they are not the paper's proofs, and
README.md and LIMITS.md state where they differ from the paper's statements. No endorsement of this repository by
the authors of the paper is claimed or implied.
